00:32:32.684 --> 00:32:34.686 align:start size:88% position:13%
Okay, fine maybe we
discounted a little bit,

00:32:34.686 --> 00:32:36.220 align:start size:84% position:16%
but now you turn on
the TV, be like, yeah,

00:32:36.220 --> 00:32:38.089
what I'm seeing is not true.

00:32:38.089 --> 00:32:40.391
What I'm seeing is not
true and people get it.

00:32:40.391 --> 00:32:42.694
- Do you miss the good liberals

00:32:42.694 --> 00:32:44.495 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we talked
about this last time,

00:32:44.495 --> 00:32:45.730
but you're a New Yorker.

00:32:45.730 --> 00:32:49.233
You grew up mostly
around liberals.

00:32:49.233 --> 00:32:52.837 align:start position:0%
I know you have a lot of
friends that are still liberals.

00:32:52.837 --> 00:32:55.907 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like, do you miss
that New York liberal,

00:32:55.907 --> 00:32:59.410
that was not sort of
the bananas lefty?

00:32:59.410 --> 00:33:01.412 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I do and it's
sort of interesting.

00:33:01.412 --> 00:33:02.780
I mean, some of them
are still that way.

00:33:02.780 --> 00:33:04.015
And honestly, some of
them are just like,

00:33:04.015 --> 00:33:05.216
"I can't believe
what's going on."

00:33:05.216 --> 00:33:06.484
I'm like, you know,

00:33:06.484 --> 00:33:08.019
the same guys that you
know have for years...

00:33:08.019 --> 00:33:10.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, obviously I'm
such a big gun guy, right?

00:33:10.088 --> 00:33:11.889
So the same guys that
for years told me,

00:33:11.889 --> 00:33:13.591
why do you need an AR-15?

00:33:13.591 --> 00:33:15.860
There's no background check,

00:33:15.860 --> 00:33:17.862
You know, Don what
AR-15 should I buy?

00:33:18.963 --> 00:33:20.198 align:start size:88% position:13%
Don, oh my God, there's
a waiting period.

00:33:20.198 --> 00:33:21.699
What's going on?

00:33:21.699 --> 00:33:22.633
I want a gun there's stuff
going on in my neighborhood.

00:33:22.633 --> 00:33:24.002
I mean, I go, "For 10 years,

00:33:24.002 --> 00:33:25.570
you told me that these
things didn't exist.

00:33:25.570 --> 00:33:28.172
Cause you had no idea, but
that was the talking point."

00:33:28.172 --> 00:33:29.707
You know,

00:33:29.707 --> 00:33:31.509
I think they're waking up to
how ridiculous it's become.

00:33:31.509 --> 00:33:33.611
So, you know, it's been a
little bit cathartic for me

00:33:33.611 --> 00:33:35.313 align:start size:97% position:3%
because you know, those
radicals that, you know, just,

00:33:35.313 --> 00:33:36.814
you literally...

00:33:36.814 --> 00:33:37.615
You know, I used to be able
to put myself in their shoes,

00:33:37.615 --> 00:33:38.850
argue their point.

00:33:38.850 --> 00:33:40.218
It's not like I stick
to a hundred percent

00:33:40.218 --> 00:33:41.419
conservative dogma.

00:33:41.419 --> 00:33:43.654
You know that in the
conversations we've had

00:33:43.654 --> 00:33:45.123
way before we even
got into politics.

00:33:45.123 --> 00:33:46.624
I'm pretty open about that.

00:33:46.624 --> 00:33:49.627
And yet, you know, I used to
be able to argue those points.

00:33:49.627 --> 00:33:52.196 align:start size:97% position:3%
I can't argue the mainstream
Democrat platform anymore

00:33:52.196 --> 00:33:53.431
with a straight
face and be like,

00:33:53.431 --> 00:33:55.400
"This is somehow
good for America."

00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:58.269 align:start size:97% position:3%
Most of them can't and that's
the problem, they see it.

00:33:58.269 --> 00:34:00.405
So there's plenty
of those Democrats.

00:34:00.405 --> 00:34:01.572 align:start size:84% position:16%
I know a bunch
that are just like,

00:34:01.572 --> 00:34:03.041
"Yeah you know,

00:34:03.041 --> 00:34:04.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
we don't love every aspect
of what you're doing,

00:34:04.542 --> 00:34:05.910
but like we believe in God,
I mean we believe in freedom.

00:34:05.910 --> 00:34:08.212 align:start size:84% position:16%
We believe in
freedom of speech."

00:34:08.212 --> 00:34:09.981 align:start size:88% position:13%
And you're listing these
things that you know,

00:34:09.981 --> 00:34:11.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said it to my convention
speech, like, you know,

00:34:11.716 --> 00:34:12.884
freedom of speech and thought

00:34:12.884 --> 00:34:16.554 align:start size:88% position:13%
that used to be a
liberal value, you know,

00:34:16.554 --> 00:34:18.089
tolerance used to
be a liberal value.

00:34:18.089 --> 00:34:19.323
I mean, they still run around.

00:34:19.323 --> 00:34:21.192
They're the party of
tolerance I'm saying,

00:34:21.192 --> 00:34:24.262
try wearing a MAGA hat
in Portland, you know,

00:34:24.262 --> 00:34:26.297
try wearing a MAGA hat in
one of these major cities.

00:34:26.297 --> 00:34:29.767
Now, if you wore a Biden hat
and I haven't seen any of them,

00:34:29.767 --> 00:34:31.969 align:start size:84% position:16%
but if someone
made one and wore--

00:34:31.969 --> 00:34:33.704 align:start size:88% position:13%
- (laughs) there's
gotta be one somewhere.

00:34:33.704 --> 00:34:35.940
- Yeah, wear it in
the most, you know,

00:34:35.940 --> 00:34:37.175
I don't wanna call
it MAGA country.

00:34:37.175 --> 00:34:38.409
That's a Jussie
Smollett special.

00:34:38.409 --> 00:34:41.579
But like, you know, in
the most conservative...

00:34:41.579 --> 00:34:43.714 line:0%
No one's gonna, they won't
even say anything to you.

00:34:43.714 --> 00:34:45.450 line:0%
They won't spit at you.

00:34:45.450 --> 00:34:47.151 line:0%
They won't throw you, they
won't beat you over the head

00:34:47.151 --> 00:34:49.287 align:start position:0% line:0%
with a brick like you're seeing
in these videos, you know,

00:34:49.287 --> 00:34:51.456 align:start size:97% position:3%
they won't loot your store,
cancel your business,

00:34:51.456 --> 00:34:55.226
or you'll get petitions going
to ruin your life on Facebook.

00:34:55.226 --> 00:34:58.129 align:start size:97% position:3%
They won't do that, but
try doing it the other way.

00:34:58.129 --> 00:35:00.031
So, you know, the party of
tolerance, isn't so tolerant.

00:35:00.031 --> 00:35:02.600 align:start position:0%
And I think a lot of
reasonable Democrats, you know,

00:35:02.600 --> 00:35:03.868
get that.

00:35:03.868 --> 00:35:05.269
I also think a lot of,
sort of that history,

00:35:05.269 --> 00:35:07.839
that blue-collar working
class, union Democrat,

00:35:07.839 --> 00:35:09.307
that had a tradition
of voting that way,

00:35:09.307 --> 00:35:10.675
I think they get it too.

00:35:10.675 --> 00:35:11.943
They're saying, what is...

00:35:11.943 --> 00:35:12.944
I used to hear it at 16.

00:35:12.944 --> 00:35:14.212
Well, you know,

00:35:14.212 --> 00:35:15.680
"Don if my grandfather
knew that I was voting

00:35:15.680 --> 00:35:17.748
for a Republican he'd be
rolling over in his grave."

00:35:17.748 --> 00:35:18.850
I go, "Well, what would he say

00:35:18.850 --> 00:35:20.251
about today's Democrat platform?

00:35:20.251 --> 00:35:21.519
Not that one."

00:35:21.519 --> 00:35:24.021
And he goes, "Huh, you
know you're right Don.

00:35:24.021 --> 00:35:25.256
Like, oh my God,"

00:35:25.256 --> 00:35:26.424 align:start size:81% position:19%
I go, "How many
genders are there?

00:35:26.424 --> 00:35:28.893
96 or two, what would he say?"

00:35:28.893 --> 00:35:30.761
You know, John F.
Kennedy, you know,

00:35:30.761 --> 00:35:33.764 align:start position:0%
this pillar of the Democrat
party, he'd be all right today,

00:35:33.764 --> 00:35:34.899
Dave, he'd be canceled.

00:35:36.334 --> 00:35:38.236 align:start size:97% position:3%
Right he'd be me too'ed and
canceled and it would be over.

00:35:38.236 --> 00:35:39.837
I mean,

00:35:39.837 --> 00:35:42.773 align:start position:0%
it's just not your grandfather's
Democrat party anymore.

00:35:42.773 --> 00:35:45.276
And I think that has
ostracized, you know,

00:35:45.276 --> 00:35:48.246 align:start size:97% position:3%
so many former Democrats where
they're starting to become,

00:35:48.246 --> 00:35:51.415
you know, either somewhat
conservative, moderate,

00:35:51.415 --> 00:35:53.584
or really, you know,
sort of libertarian

00:35:53.584 --> 00:35:56.420
in many of their views, which
are so many of my views too.

00:35:56.420 --> 00:35:57.922
- Yeah, I hear you, man.

00:35:57.922 --> 00:35:59.824
And we've had many
discussions about it.

00:35:59.824 --> 00:36:01.893 align:start size:97% position:3%
Let's jump to a private
discussion we had about it.

00:36:01.893 --> 00:36:05.129 align:start size:88% position:13%
Cause I think it'll
get to something
really interesting here

00:36:05.129 --> 00:36:07.231 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is, my audience
has heard it,

00:36:07.231 --> 00:36:10.968 align:start size:97% position:3%
but one night, you and
Kimberly invited David and I

00:36:10.968 --> 00:36:12.637
to dinner at Mar-a-Lago.

00:36:12.637 --> 00:36:13.871
We had a really nice dinner.

00:36:13.871 --> 00:36:17.642 align:start size:88% position:13%
We argued about politics
for two, three hours.

00:36:17.642 --> 00:36:19.177
I had a couple of drinks.

00:36:19.177 --> 00:36:21.546
You do not drink so I'm not
sure who won the arguments,

00:36:21.546 --> 00:36:24.282
but we did about three hours
there and then at the end,

00:36:24.282 --> 00:36:25.750 align:start size:81% position:19%
your dad was there
and by the way,

00:36:25.750 --> 00:36:27.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
this was right at the
beginning of impeachment.

00:36:27.585 --> 00:36:29.420 align:start size:88% position:13%
And everybody said, "The
walls are closing in,

00:36:29.420 --> 00:36:30.655
he's freaking out,"

00:36:30.655 --> 00:36:32.557
but the guy is sitting
there, he has no tie on.

00:36:32.557 --> 00:36:34.559 align:start size:97% position:3%
He was with Giuliani and
some people and he's laughing

00:36:34.559 --> 00:36:35.793
and having fun.

00:36:35.793 --> 00:36:36.994
Anyway, at the end
of dinner, you said,

00:36:36.994 --> 00:36:38.496 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Hey, would you like
to meet my dad?"

00:36:38.496 --> 00:36:40.498
And I was like, "Yeah, I'd
like to meet the president.

00:36:40.498 --> 00:36:42.033
Let's do it."

00:36:42.033 --> 00:36:45.069
And you introduce us and then
he turns to David and he says,

00:36:45.069 --> 00:36:46.270
"Well, who are you?"

00:36:46.270 --> 00:36:47.772 align:start size:84% position:16%
And David says, "Well,
I'm his husband,"

00:36:47.772 --> 00:36:50.508
and your dad immediately,
like there was no pause,

00:36:50.508 --> 00:36:52.877
he clapped his hands together,
he slapped them on the table.

00:36:52.877 --> 00:36:55.213 align:start size:88% position:13%
He said, "That's great,
that's just great.

00:36:55.213 --> 00:36:57.048
I wanna stand up and
shake your hands."

00:36:57.048 --> 00:36:58.549
He shakes our hands, he says,

00:36:58.549 --> 00:37:00.618
"The only thing wrong with you
guys is you're too handsome.

00:37:00.618 --> 00:37:01.986
Melania, can you believe it?

00:37:01.986 --> 00:37:03.588 align:start size:81% position:19%
These handsome
guys are married."

00:37:03.588 --> 00:37:06.090
And it was just so obvious to me

00:37:06.090 --> 00:37:10.261 align:start size:97% position:3%
that in this completely
unscripted, unplanned moment

00:37:10.261 --> 00:37:12.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
where you just
brought us up to him,

00:37:12.129 --> 00:37:13.864
that he actually said,

00:37:13.864 --> 00:37:15.132
I don't know if he
wants me to say it,

00:37:15.132 --> 00:37:16.334
but I've said it before.

00:37:16.334 --> 00:37:18.202
He said, "I want you
guys to know something.

00:37:18.202 --> 00:37:21.305 align:start position:0%
I don't give a shit and I don't
think anyone's given a shit

00:37:21.305 --> 00:37:22.573
in 20 years,"

00:37:22.573 --> 00:37:24.675 align:start size:84% position:16%
talking about gay
marriage or whatever.

00:37:26.310 --> 00:37:29.780
How do you get over the
labels when it comes

00:37:29.780 --> 00:37:30.715
to something like that?

00:37:30.715 --> 00:37:32.283
Just the base stuff your dad is,

00:37:32.283 --> 00:37:36.554 align:start size:97% position:3%
or your family is homophobic
or they're racist.

00:37:36.554 --> 00:37:38.990
Cause no matter how many
times I tell that story,

00:37:38.990 --> 00:37:40.358
people say I'm a
sell out somehow

00:37:40.358 --> 00:37:43.995
or some version of
some of that stuff.

00:37:43.995 --> 00:37:45.496
- The reality is this,

00:37:45.496 --> 00:37:47.465
Donald Trump is the first person

00:37:47.465 --> 00:37:49.967
to run for president
of the United States,

00:37:49.967 --> 00:37:53.604
and when he ran, he
was for gay marriage.

00:37:53.604 --> 00:37:55.206
I mean, Obama was against it

00:37:55.206 --> 00:37:56.807
because he was told he
had to be against it

00:37:56.807 --> 00:37:58.909
and maybe he wasn't in
his actual convictions.

00:37:58.909 --> 00:38:01.245 align:start size:97% position:3%
But as part of his
platform, he was against it

00:38:01.245 --> 00:38:03.514 align:start size:84% position:16%
because that's what
they had to do, right.

00:38:03.514 --> 00:38:04.749
You listen to the talking points

00:38:04.749 --> 00:38:06.417
and you must succumb to them.

00:38:06.417 --> 00:38:08.419 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, you know, again,
Donald, Trump's

00:38:08.419 --> 00:38:09.620
been way ahead of that curve.

00:38:09.620 --> 00:38:10.454
I think we have...

00:38:10.454 --> 00:38:11.389
We're from New York.

00:38:11.389 --> 00:38:12.723
I mean, it's like, (laughs)

00:38:12.723 --> 00:38:14.458
a pretty big percentage
of the people around us

00:38:14.458 --> 00:38:16.060
at any given time are probably.

00:38:16.060 --> 00:38:18.796
We just don't care what
you do in your own bed.

00:38:18.796 --> 00:38:19.630
Who gives a shit?

00:38:19.630 --> 00:38:21.299
No one's gonna care.

00:38:21.299 --> 00:38:22.466 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's one of those
issues you're right.

00:38:22.466 --> 00:38:24.068 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, we're already
there, frankly,

00:38:24.068 --> 00:38:26.937
but in 20 years it'll be
even different, right.

00:38:26.937 --> 00:38:28.339
Even more so, I mean,

00:38:28.339 --> 00:38:30.441 align:start size:97% position:3%
even some of the older
school people that, you know,

00:38:30.441 --> 00:38:33.644
may be a little bit more, you
know, just kinda read the,

00:38:33.644 --> 00:38:35.646 align:start size:84% position:16%
sort of the older
religious dogma on it.

00:38:35.646 --> 00:38:37.148
Like no one cares.

00:38:37.148 --> 00:38:39.283
Even the people that say they
care, no, they don't care.

00:38:39.283 --> 00:38:40.618 align:start size:88% position:13%
They sort of, they feel
obligated to do it.

00:38:40.618 --> 00:38:42.153
Donald Trump just had
the guts to be like,

00:38:42.153 --> 00:38:43.387
"Hey, I don't care.

00:38:43.387 --> 00:38:44.822 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm running for the
Republican nomination.

00:38:44.822 --> 00:38:46.324
This is not an issue
for me whatsoever.

00:38:46.324 --> 00:38:47.758
Go ahead, have at it."

00:38:47.758 --> 00:38:49.960 align:start size:97% position:3%
I always joke that the
best wedding I ever went to

00:38:49.960 --> 00:38:52.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
was a gay wedding because
it was on a Tuesday.

00:38:52.096 --> 00:38:53.698
They were like, "Well, we don't
wanna screw up your weekend.

00:38:53.698 --> 00:38:54.732
We're just gonna have
fun on a Tuesday."

00:38:54.732 --> 00:38:55.900 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean that's perfect.
(laughs)

00:38:55.900 --> 00:38:57.702 align:start size:84% position:16%
But this is the
greatest wedding ever.

00:38:57.702 --> 00:38:59.236 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't have to lose
my whole weekend.

00:38:59.236 --> 00:39:00.905
That's awesome, I love you guys.

00:39:00.905 --> 00:39:03.274
And so, you know, he
has a kid, but again,

00:39:03.274 --> 00:39:04.375
you see it every day.

00:39:04.375 --> 00:39:05.876
Donald Trump has been so proud.

00:39:05.876 --> 00:39:07.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you guys didn't
have a problem with Obama,

00:39:07.545 --> 00:39:11.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
literally running against
gay marriage in 2008.

00:39:12.783 --> 00:39:16.253
But Donald Trump runs
as a conservative,

00:39:16.253 --> 00:39:18.189 align:start size:84% position:16%
literally going
against the, you know,

00:39:18.189 --> 00:39:19.890 align:start size:84% position:16%
the more traditional
dogma and again,

00:39:19.890 --> 00:39:22.059
I don't think it's a party
platform issue at this point.

00:39:22.059 --> 00:39:23.294
Like I said, I don't
think anyone cares,

00:39:23.294 --> 00:39:24.462 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they probably
haven't for a while,

00:39:24.462 --> 00:39:26.664 align:start size:84% position:16%
but he literally
said, "I don't care."

00:39:26.664 --> 00:39:27.765
Well, you know, guess what?

00:39:27.765 --> 00:39:28.966
You know, you're a Republican,

00:39:28.966 --> 00:39:30.468 align:start size:88% position:13%
you're trying and to
get the evangelical vote

00:39:30.468 --> 00:39:32.203
and you still say, "Hey,
I don't care about that."

00:39:32.203 --> 00:39:33.938
Let people live and let live.

00:39:33.938 --> 00:39:38.008
I mean the Republican party is
the true party of tolerance.

00:39:38.008 --> 00:39:39.343
Now that doesn't mean, you know,

00:39:39.343 --> 00:39:40.845
I've been open about this too

00:39:40.845 --> 00:39:42.413
and it doesn't mean I don't
draw the line some places,

00:39:42.413 --> 00:39:44.615 align:start size:84% position:16%
again I don't care
how you even identify.

00:39:44.615 --> 00:39:47.885 align:start size:97% position:3%
Where I start to care is when
you know you're six, two,

00:39:47.885 --> 00:39:50.421 align:start size:97% position:3%
285 and jacked then you
decide you wanna be a woman

00:39:50.421 --> 00:39:53.257 align:start size:97% position:3%
and compete against, you
know, my daughter is sports.

00:39:53.257 --> 00:39:56.761
You know identify how you want,

00:39:56.761 --> 00:39:59.196 align:start size:97% position:3%
but you start taking her
scholarship, I have a problem.

00:39:59.196 --> 00:40:01.599
I wonder where the people who
fought for title nine are,

00:40:01.599 --> 00:40:02.833 align:start size:84% position:16%
how come they
won't say anything.

00:40:02.833 --> 00:40:04.068
But it's interesting
when I've come out

00:40:04.068 --> 00:40:05.302
on some of those
things and again,

00:40:05.302 --> 00:40:06.237
I don't give a crap if
you're trans or not,

00:40:06.237 --> 00:40:07.037
that makes no difference to me.

00:40:07.037 --> 00:40:08.439
It's when you sort of...

00:40:08.439 --> 00:40:09.874
Let's have the best.

00:40:09.874 --> 00:40:12.076 align:start size:97% position:3%
Let's take a female athlete
who's top of her game,

00:40:12.076 --> 00:40:13.377
who's worked her whole life.

00:40:13.377 --> 00:40:14.745
I'm a journeyman male athlete.

00:40:14.745 --> 00:40:16.347
It's not working out so
well congratulations.

00:40:16.347 --> 00:40:17.848
I'm gonna flip it, now
I'm a state champion.

00:40:17.848 --> 00:40:19.283
I'm getting your scholarship.

